@startuml events_dispatch
title Internal events and inbox creation
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "hermes (CLI / TUI)" as Client
participant "hermes-document-service" as HDS
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

participant "Outbox worker\n(hermes-document-service)" as Publisher
queue "Apache Kafka" as Bus
participant "hermes-notification-service" as Handler
== Change domain state ==
User -> Client : Perform a modifying operation
Client -> HDS : Command(session, expected_version)
group Single transaction
  HDS -> DB : Check permissions, constraints and version
  HDS -> DB : Save domain changes and outbox events
end
HDS --> Client : Success after commit or error without events

== Publish asynchronously ==
Publisher -> DB : Read unpublished outbox events
Publisher -> Bus : Publish(event_id, type, schema_version, payload)
Bus --> Publisher : Acknowledgement
Publisher -> DB : Mark published after acknowledgement
note over Publisher, Bus
  A crash between publication and marking may cause redelivery.
end note

== Convert events into notifications ==
Bus -> Handler : Internal event
Handler -> Handler : Select users / workspaces / documents policy
Handler -> DB : Read recipients, preferences and current permissions
Handler -> Handler : Exclude deleted users, disabled categories and actor\n(except ProfileChanged); merge reasons per recipient
loop For each eligible recipient
  Handler -> DB : Transaction: insert notification\nUNIQUE(recipient_id, source_event_id); duplicate is a no-op
end
Handler -> Bus : Acknowledge after all results are persisted
note over Handler, DB
  Retry failures without losing or duplicating inbox items.
  Events without user relevance create no notifications.
  WorkspaceDeleted, WorkspaceMemberRemoved and DocumentDeleted
  permit minimal notices under their specific recipient policies.
end note
@enduml
